1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,240
AquaShift. Solar power into water. Water stored for later.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:12,298
When solar would otherwise be curtailed, the idea is to use
it for desalination, where plant and grid conditions allow.

3
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:20,202
Make fresh water during that window. Store it in
a tank. Use the water later, when people need it.

4
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:29,498
That's the concept. These are illustrations. No real
curtailed solar has been recovered by this prototype.

5
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:38,194
Here is the working draft. Choose a date, change
the tank size, and inspect the proposed schedule.

6
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,607
Same water. Same energy. In this scenario, the
cost falls because of the assumed hourly prices.

7
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:56,562
With less storage, there is less room to shift production. Water supply still comes first.

8
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:05,206
In average error, the reference loses to the stronger
simple control. Added AI value is unproven.

9
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:14,318
Sites tests an irrigation budget and an injected leak. The meter data is simulated.

10
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:23,449
Next: real grid signals, plant limits, water demand and tariffs. Then test the benefit.

11
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:29,646
Loucas's concept. Stefanos's expanded roadmap. An AI-assisted draft.
